# Frontend organization (`apps/app`)

Default to **feature-based organization**.

## Directory structure (defaults)

- `apps/app/app/`: Next.js App Router (routes only)
- `apps/app/features/`: feature modules (most code goes here)
- `apps/app/components/`: shared primitives only (cross-feature)
- `apps/app/hooks/`: shared hooks only (cross-feature)
- `apps/app/lib/`: infrastructure/config
- `apps/app/utils/`: pure utilities (no React/framework deps)

## Feature module contract (hybrid barrel policy)

- **Required**: `apps/app/features/<feature>/index.ts` defines the feature’s public API.
- **OK**: feature-scoped barrels only.
- **Avoid**: “mega barrels” that re-export large parts of the repo.

Example:

```typescript
// apps/app/features/auth/index.ts
export { SignUpForm, SignInForm } from "./components";
export { useSignUp } from "./hooks";
```

## When to abstract

- **Logic used in 1 component**: keep inline.
- **Logic used in 2+ components (same feature)**: `features/<feature>/hooks/*`.
- **Logic used across features**: `apps/app/hooks/*`.
- **Pure util**: `apps/app/utils/*` or `features/<feature>/utils/*`.

## Import patterns

- **Prefer**: `import { X } from "@/features/<feature>"` (feature public API)
- **Avoid**: importing another feature’s internals like `@/features/<feature>/components/...`

